<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Midgaard</h1>
<p>Midgaard is the great capital of Valhalla. It has been part of the game 
since the very first DikuMUD, and its name comes from Norse mythology. 
New players begin in Udgaard, but sooner or later everyone comes to 
Midgaard.
</p><p>What you find there:
</p>
<ul><li>the Cathedral, in the north of the city;</li>
<li>shops of every kind: magic, tailor, pets, leather, ironmonger, baker, greengrocer, butcher, boats, fish, armour, mortician, blacksmith, carpenter, weaponsmith and jeweller;</li>
<li>the bank and the item storage;</li>
<li>inns: the Grunting Boar, Filthy's and the Park Cafe;</li>
<li>the guild halls of the fighters, healers, thieves and conjurers, where new players train, and of the paladins and the sorcerers; the dark knights meet below, through the sewers;</li>
<li>the city guard and its Captain, who keeps the city's law (see <a cmd='#'>Help Laws</a>).</li></ul>
<p>Roads lead out of the city to the King's Road, the Etz-Nab woods, the 
palace, the Cypress Forest and the moor. Type <a cmd='#'>help area</a> while you are 
in Midgaard to see a map of the city drawn in letters, with where 
everything is; the web client also shows a map of it (see <a cmd='#'>Help Map</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
